Z||000003||86seyellow||09-04-2001||12:03 AM||||check a cylinder. I did all the same as you did, then I didi a compression test, found out #3 was not firing. I bought a new crate engine rather than a rebuild. <P>------------------<BR>if you saw a yellow streak go by you really fast it was a fiero<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||09-04-2001||10:09 AM||||As posted above, recheck the firing order/plugwires.  If that doesn't help, I would eliminate a burnt valve by taking a compression check.  I just resolved my intermittant mis-fire problem. I intended to change injectors and put on a fuel rail which I rebuilt.  I figured while I have it apart take the plugs out for a plug reading and found two had a wierd crack/hole in the insulator around the center electrode and a third the center electrode was shifted over almost all the way to the side but still tight (not loose or broken).  These plugs had a 1000 miles on them.  I think this was caused by detonation as the injectors were very bad and the heads had been shaved (real good) by the previous owner's mechanic.  When I put it all back together, it purred like a 'smooth engine' but I hear it pinging on 89 octane gas.  Anyway, keep at it it is solveable (new word).  GL<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GTZ34||09-05-2001||09:21 AM||||Curtis,  You've changed almost everything... You may have changed them but didn't mention it, did you put in fresh plugs after flooding it?  If not, that is a cheap test/fix and make sure you gap them of course.  Also, did you get a chance to take a compression test?  If you have a weak cylinder or two try driving it some for a while (1000 mi if you can take it) then repeat the check.  If a valve was in the open position for a while it may have surface corrosion that will clean up as you drive it.  One last thought, is it possible that you picked up some bad gas that originally caused your car to die in the first place?  GL||||reg||1
